*OpenGroup: General/General
*OpenUI *Resolution/Resolution: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 20 AnySetup *Resolution
*DefaultResolution: 360dpi
*Resolution 360dpi/Standard 360 x 360 dpi: "<</HWResolution[360 360]>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *Resolution

*OpenUI *ColorModel/Color Mode: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 10 AnySetup *ColorModel
*DefaultColorModel: Gray
*ColorModel Gray/Black and white: "<</cupsColorSpace 0/cupsColorOrder 0/cupsBitsPerColor 8>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *ColorModel
*CloseGroup: General

*OpenGroup: Label/Label Options
*% Check boxes, so the modes can be combined. Half cut wins if both cuts are ticked,
*% neither ticked means no cut. These are the DRIVER SETTINGS: the settings app changes
*% their defaults with lpadmin and the filter reads them from this file ($PPD). The
*% standard "Flip horizontally" box also mirrors (macOS flips the page itself).
*OpenUI *HalfCut/Half cut (cut the label, keep the backing paper): Boolean
*OrderDependency: 30 AnySetup *HalfCut
*DefaultHalfCut: True
*HalfCut True/Half cut: "<<>>setpagedevice"
*HalfCut False/Off: "<<>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *HalfCut

*OpenUI *FullCut/Full cut (cut through the label and the backing paper): Boolean
*OrderDependency: 31 AnySetup *FullCut
*DefaultFullCut: False
*FullCut True/Full cut: "<<>>setpagedevice"
*FullCut False/Off: "<<>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *FullCut

*OpenUI *Chain/Chain printing (no feed or cut at the end, for continuous labels): Boolean
*OrderDependency: 32 AnySetup *Chain
*DefaultChain: False
*Chain True/Chain printing: "<<>>setpagedevice"
*Chain False/Off: "<<>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *Chain

*OpenUI *MirrorPrint/Mirror print (to read through a clear label): Boolean
*OrderDependency: 33 AnySetup *MirrorPrint
*DefaultMirrorPrint: False
*MirrorPrint True/Mirror print: "<<>>setpagedevice"
*MirrorPrint False/Off: "<<>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *MirrorPrint
*CloseGroup: Label

*OpenGroup: Quality/Print Quality
*OpenUI *LabelQuality/Print Quality: PickOne
*OrderDependency: 25 AnySetup *LabelQuality
*DefaultLabelQuality: Normal
*LabelQuality Normal/Normal (360 x 360 dpi): "<</HWResolution[360 360]>>setpagedevice"
*LabelQuality High/High quality (slower, same resolution): "<</HWResolution[360 360]>>setpagedevice"
*LabelQuality HiRes/High resolution (360 x 720 dpi, slowest): "<</HWResolution[720 720]>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *LabelQuality
*CloseGroup: Quality

